{"retractions" [[17592186156983 :question/worked-solution "Suppose $f(x), g(x), h(x)$ and $k(x)$ are functions and $c$ is a nonzero constant. Then, we have the following properties of Big-O notation.\n\n- The sum and product properties. If\n\n$$\nf = \\mathcal O(h)\\quad\\textrm{and}\\quad g = \\mathcal O(k)\\quad\\textrm{as}\\quad x\\to a,\n$$\n\nthen\n\n$$\nf+g = \\mathcal O(h+k)\\quad\\textrm{and}\\quad fg = \\mathcal O(hk)\\quad\\textrm{as}\\quad x\\to a.\n$$\n\n- The constant multiple property. If\n\n$$\nf = \\mathcal O(cg)\\quad\\textrm{as}\\quad x\\to a,\n$$\n\nthen\n\n$$\nf = \\mathcal O(g)\\quad\\textrm{as}\\quad x\\to a.\n$$\n\n- The reflexive property.\n\n$$\nf = \\mathcal O(f)\\quad\\textrm{as}\\quad x\\to a.\n$$\n\n- The transitive property. If\n\n$$\nf = \\mathcal O(g) \\quad\\textrm{and}\\quad g = \\mathcal O(h)\\quad\\textrm{as}\\quad x\\to a,\n$$\n\nthen\n\n$$\nf = \\mathcal O(h)\\quad\\textrm{as}\\quad x\\to a.\n$$\n\n- The absorption property. If\n\n$$\nf = \\mathcal O(g+h)\\quad\\textrm{and}\\quad g = \\mathcal O(h)\\quad\\textrm{as}\\quad x\\to a,\n$$\n\nthen\n\n$$\nf = \\mathcal O(h)\\quad\\textrm{as}\\quad x\\to a.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let us justify each selected step.\n\n- We first consider line  $\\textrm{L3}.$ From line $\\textrm{L1}$ we have\n\n$$\ne^{x} = \\mathcal O(1)\\quad\\textrm{as}\\quad x\\to 0,\n$$\n\nand from line $\\textrm{L2}$ we have\n\n$$\n\\sec x = \\mathcal O(1)\\quad\\textrm{as}\\quad x\\to 0.\n$$\n\nThus, by lines $\\bbox[4pt,border:solid 1pt gainsboro]{\\text{L1 and L3}}$ and $\\bbox[4pt,border:solid 1pt gainsboro]{\\text{the sum property}},$ we obtain\n\n$$\nf = \\mathcal O(1+1) = \\mathcal O(2)\\quad\\textrm{as}\\quad x\\to 0.\n$$\n\n- Finally, we consider line $\\textrm{L4}.$ From line $\\bbox[4pt,border:solid 1pt gainsboro]{\\text{L4}}$ we have\n\n$$\nf = \\mathcal O(2)\\quad\\textrm{as}\\quad x\\to 0.\n$$\n\nSince $2$ is just a constant multiple of $1,$ it follows by $\\bbox[4pt,border:solid 1pt gainsboro]{\\text{the constant multiple property}}$ that\n\n$$\nf = \\mathcal O(1)\\quad\\textrm{as}\\quad x\\to 0.\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" []}
